& [IR8IntegratedManagerFixtureTraceAndFaultPlanV1] is the IR8-S04 fixture, trace, and fault plan for integrated manager orchestration
  + [fixture_plan_id] is ir8-integrated-manager-fixture-trace-and-fault-plan-v1
  + [fixture_plan_uuid] is d5d2d1cb-1f32-402b-9573-15b220313a0f
  + [slice_id] is IR8-S04
  + [source_chunk] is IR8 integrated manager orchestration planning
  + [authority_scope] is fixture case inventory, trace expectations, fault expectations, generated-output future boundary, and no-live-effect fixture planning
  + [implementation_scope] is fixture and expected-ledger plan only
  + [model_route_used] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable

  = must: define fixture cases and expected trace/fault ledgers without creating fixture files, expected ledger files, generated outputs, implementation code, adapters, transports, UI, dependencies, package metadata, dispatch, operations control, or live machine control
  = must: cover ready, blocked, stale, contested, unsafe, ambiguous, generated-output, graph-checkpoint, dry-run, human override, and live-control refusal paths
  = must: preserve authority_notice, freshness_state, source_ref_set, proof_obligation_set, completion_gate, support_delta, requirement_delta, and fault_record expectations in every applicable fixture
  = should: route future fixture file creation and deterministic expected ledger drafting to GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark after IR8 implementation activation explicitly opens it

& [IR8IntegratedManagerFixtureCaseSet] is the planned fixture case set for integrated manager orchestration
  + [fixture_case] is IR8M-001 accepted-source-ready-work-packet
    + [purpose] is prove manager can classify accepted source authority, current readiness, and clean support into a ready_for_claim work packet candidate
    + [expected_trace] is authority_classification, freshness_check, support_check, readiness_projection_ready, proof_obligation_attached, completion_gate_attached, and work_packet_candidate_ready_for_claim
    + [expected_fault] is none
  + [fixture_case] is IR8M-002 stale-boundary-input-blocks-ready-packet
    + [purpose] is prove stale proof pack, slice surface, or readiness surface blocks false-ready work
    + [expected_trace] is authority_classification, freshness_check_stale, stale_work_notice, proof_obligation_failed, and SOP_first_interrupt_context
    + [expected_fault] is stale_boundary_input
  + [fixture_case] is IR8M-003 unsupported-requirement-blocks-packet
    + [purpose] is prove unresolved support_gap prevents ready output
    + [expected_trace] is support_gap_detected, readiness_projection_blocked, blocked_work_notice, and completion_gate_not_opened
    + [expected_fault] is unsupported_requirement
  + [fixture_case] is IR8M-004 contested-coordination-claim-interrupts
    + [purpose] is prove incompatible active claims block or interrupt packet readiness without collapsing conversation identities
    + [expected_trace] is coordination_claim_classified, contested_claim_detected, contested_work_notice, and SOP_first_interrupt_context
    + [expected_fault] is contested_coordination_claim
  + [fixture_case] is IR8M-005 mailbox-carrier-is-not-authority
    + [purpose] is prove mailbox or rendezvous carrier context can inform review but cannot accept source authority, completion, dispatch, or live effects
    + [expected_trace] is carrier_context_classified, authority_notice_attached, lower_tier_context_preserved, and no_authority_promotion
    + [expected_fault] is none
  + [fixture_case] is IR8M-006 surface-action-request-requires-classification
    + [purpose] is prove chat, UI, terminal, IRC, Matrix, web, or Codex action requests are classified before affecting readiness
    + [expected_trace] is surface_action_request_received, carrier_context_classified, requested_effect_classified, safe_route_or_interrupt_selected
    + [expected_fault] is unclassified_authority_sensitive_record when classification basis is missing
  + [fixture_case] is IR8M-007 dry-run-success-not-dispatch-authority
    + [purpose] is prove dry-run success can inform readiness only as operations planning evidence and cannot dispatch jobs or authorize live control
    + [expected_trace] is operation_dry_run_result_classified, no_live_effect_notice_attached, readiness_evidence_recorded, dispatch_refused
    + [expected_fault] is dry_run_to_live_control_promotion when promotion is attempted
  + [fixture_case] is IR8M-008 human-override-scoped-revocable
    + [purpose] is prove human override handoff requires scope, freshness, revocation route, risk context, and explicit authority notice
    + [expected_trace] is human_override_request_classified, freshness_checked, scope_checked, revocation_route_checked, override_record_contextualized
    + [expected_fault] is human_override_required when override is missing or stale
  + [fixture_case] is IR8M-009 generated-projection-not-authority
    + [purpose] is prove generated reports, surface projections, fixture outputs, and disposable manager projections cannot become source authority
    + [expected_trace] is generated_projection_classified, authority_notice_attached, source_authority_requirement_preserved, promotion_refused
    + [expected_fault] is generated_output_authority_promotion when promotion is attempted
  + [fixture_case] is IR8M-010 graph-checkpoint-not-authority
    + [purpose] is prove graph checkpoint state can resume procedure state but cannot define source truth or readiness alone
    + [expected_trace] is checkpoint_context_classified, kernel_reference_checked, source_authority_required, checkpoint_authority_promotion_refused
    + [expected_fault] is graph_checkpoint_authority_promotion when promotion is attempted
  + [fixture_case] is IR8M-011 live-control-request-refused
    + [purpose] is prove live-control, process, GPU, model runtime, job, credential, network, and destructive filesystem requests refuse without separate accepted authority
    + [expected_trace] is requested_effect_classified_live_control, safety_boundary_checked, missing_live_authority_detected, refusal_record_emitted
    + [expected_fault] is requested_forbidden_scope
  + [fixture_case] is IR8M-012 model-route-required
    + [purpose] is prove every work packet candidate states GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable or requires deeper reasoning
    + [expected_trace] is model_route_checked, missing_route_refused, ready_packet_requires_route
    + [expected_fault] is model_route_ambiguity when missing

